  "problem": "| $z$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-0.3\\,$ | $\\,0.3745\\,$ | $\\,0.3707\\,$ | $\\,0.3669\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.2\\,$ | $\\,0.4129\\,$ | $\\,0.4090\\,$ | $\\,0.4052\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.1\\,$ | $\\,0.4522\\,$ | $\\,0.4483\\,$ | $\\,0.4443\\,$ |\n\nApproximate the value of $z$ such that $P(Z\\le z)=0.3725$ using interval bisection and the above table\n\n$z\u2248$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "First, we find the two numbers in the table that $0.3725$ lies between. These numbers are $0.3707$ and $0.3745.$ So, we have the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.3707 & <0.3725<0.3745\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above inequality in terms of $\u03a6,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u03a6(-0.33) & <\u03a6(z)<\u03a6(-0.32).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, using interval bisection, we can approximate $z$ as\n\n$$\nz\u2248\\frac{-0.33+(-0.32)}{2}=-0.325.\n$$",
